});
```

The one fork worth deciding now: whether "a few hundred a month" stays true for the next year or two. If growth stays in that range, this is the whole solution — no Elasticsearch/Meilisearch, no separate index to keep in sync. If you're expecting an order-of-magnitude jump (bulk catalog imports, multi-tenant sellers), that's the point to introduce a dedicated search service instead of retrofitting one later. Fuzzy/typo tolerance (`pg_trgm`) is the next layer down if exact-word matching proves too strict.

At 38k rows growing slowly, this is a Postgres full-text search problem, not a case for standing up Elasticsearch/Meilisearch — no new infra, and it'll stay fast for years at this scale.

